nodecode-decisions is a rewrite of eve-ai-dev's eve-ai-dev/hermes-decisions-plugin:

  https://github.com/eve-ai-dev/hermes-decisions-plugin
  commit eeac2eac98a3d1f566dc020912bb378aece431f8
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Decisions maintainers (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the two tools (decisions_submit, decisions_status) with their JSON boundaries, the predicate-only
request shape and its field-by-field reply check, the choice of background or foreground, the job registry
with its ceiling of four running and its memory of thirty-two finished, the ownership of a job by the home
and session that started it, and the section (endpoint, model, key, timeout) as a Nodecode section — in
Common Lisp, on NLK:HTTP, with nothing of the Python package bundled.

Left out, and why: the scoped-secret indirection (credential_ref plus the credential_endpoint binding that
must equal endpoint) is one setting here, because a Nodecode section is the operator's approval and has no
second place to name a secret; the key is api_key written inline or api_key_env naming the variable. The
"notification_accepted" member of a job is gone: it reported Hermes injecting a message into a running
session, and here the model polls decisions_status or the operator reads /decisions. Redirects follow
NLK:HTTP's own five rather than being refused at the first hop. The completion notice Hermes posted into
the session is not posted either: a cell's notice is a toast for the operator, and a job that finished is
read where it is asked for.
